<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5715" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιβαίνω</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-βήσομαι,</span> etc.:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>go about</i> or <i>around,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠέλιος μέσον οὐρανὸν
			ἀμφιβεβήκει</span> sun <i>in his course had reached</i>
			mid-heaven, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				8.68
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>bestride,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφ᾽ ἑνὶ δούρατι βαῖνε</span>
			<i>he bestrode</i> a beam, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				5.371
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππον ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Del.</u>
					113
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. θηλείαις,</span> of a cock,
				<i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				5.8
			</span></i>: esp., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>bestride</i> a fallen friend, <i>so as to protect</i> him, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφὶ κασιγνήτῳ βεβαώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.477
				</span></i>
			: hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> of
			tutelary deities, <i>guard, protect,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χρύσην ἀμφιβέβηκας</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1.37
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίμονες ἀμφιβάντες πόλιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					175
				</span></i>
			:—so, of a wild beast, <i>guard</i> its young,
				<i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				3.218
			</span></i>; or its prey, X <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				10.13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>surround, encompass,</i> c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεφέλη σκόπελον ἀμφιβέβηκε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					12.74
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὲ πόνος φρένας ἀμφιβέβηκεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.355
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.541
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταραγμὸν ἀμφιβάντ᾽ εἶχον μάχης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1406
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ μοῖρα . . οἵα με . . ἀμφιβᾶσ᾽
					ἔχεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					1082
				</span></i>
			: c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρώων νέφος ἀμφιβέβηκε νηυσίν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.66
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀμφί τι,</span> of a slit
			bandage which <i>embraces</i> a tender part without pressing on
			it, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				33
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόδε μοι θράσος ἀμφιβαίνει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					609
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιβᾶσα φλὸξ οἴνου,</span>
			metaph. from flame <i>spreading round</i> a vessel on the fire,
				<i><span class="en">
				<u>Alc.</u>
				758
			</span></i>.</div>
